.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a command-line utility for Advent of Code.
It exposes its functionality via three commands:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Cm a ,
.Cm answer :
submits an answer
.It
.Cm c ,
.Cm calendar :
displays a calendar
.It
.Cm p ,
.Cm puzzle :
downloads a puzzle
.El
.Pp
There is no default command.
.
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl s
.Ar file No \&|
.Fl "-session"
.Ar file
.Xc
A path to a text file containing the session ID associated with
a logged in Advent of Code user.
The file must exist.
Without this option,
.Nm
uses the file described in CONFIGURATION below.
.It Xo
.Fl v No \&|
.Fl "-version"
.Xc
Print the version of
.Nm
and exit.
.El
.Pp
For
.Nm
.Cm answer ,
the following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl d
.Ar day No \&|
.Fl "-day"
.Ar day
.Xc
The day of the year for Advent of Code.
During the Advent of Code competition period,
this defaults to the day of the period.
It otherwise defaults to
.Ql "1" .
.It Xo
.Fl p
.Ar part No \&|
.Fl "-part"
.Ar part
.Xc
The part of the puzzle.
This defaults to
.Ql "1" .
.It Xo
.Fl y
.Ar year No \&|
.Fl "-year"
.Ar year
.Xc
The year for Advent of Code.
This defaults to the most recent year of the competition.
Prior to December,
this will be the previous year.
Once the competition begins,
it defaults to the current year.
.El
.Pp
