.El
.Pp
For
.Nm
.Cm puzzle ,
the following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl S No \&|
.Fl "-no-subdirs"
.Xc
Save files in the current working directory and not in subdirectories.
By default,
.Nm
creates a subdirectory of the format
.Ql "day<nn>"
where
.Ql "<nn>"
is a two-digit representation of the day in the period.
The puzzle is saved as
.Ql "puzzle\&.txt"
and the input is saved as
.Ql "input\&.txt" .
When this flag is set,
.Nm
instead saves the puzzle to
.Ql "day<nn>\&.puzzle"
and the input to
.Ql "day<nn>\&.input" .
.It Xo
.Fl d
.Ar day No \&|
.Fl "-day"
.Ar day
.Xc
The day of the year for Advent of Code.
During the Advent of Code competition period,
this defaults to the day of the period.
It otherwise defaults to
.Ql "1" .
.It Xo
.Fl w
.Ar cols No \&|
.Fl "-wrap"
.Ar cols
.Xc
Wrap the text of the puzzle at
.Ar cols
columns.
Paragraphs and list items are wrapped,
and the lines that continue a list item are indented to align
with its text.
Code blocks are not wrapped.
By default,
.Nm
does not wrap the text.
