.Sh CONFIGURATION
Advent of Code does not expose a proper API for tools like
.Nm .
As a result,
.Nm
interacts with the Advent of Code server using the session ID
of a logged in user.
To obtain your session ID do the following:
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
log in to Advent of Code
.It
open your browser’s developer tools
.It
go to the Storage tab
.It
find the cookie named
.Ql "session"
.It
copy its value
.El
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
reads the session ID from
.Eo
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sled/session.txt
.Ec ,
or from
.Eo
.Pa ~/.config/sled/session.txt
.Ec
if
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
If that file does not exist and standard input is a terminal,
.Nm
asks for the session ID,
saves it to that file,
readable only by the user,
and continues.
Otherwise it exits with an error.
.Pp
To use a different file,
pass its path to
.Fl "-session" .
A file in the current working directory is read only when given
this way.
.
